DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((e^(x)))^(1/2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("(e^(x))^3");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-4, 0} U {-4, 0} U {-5, -4} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-5, -4} U ((-infinity, 10])");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-5, -4} U ((((-infinity, 10] U (-infinity, 10]))) U {-4, 0}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[0, 12] U [0, 12]");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[0, 12] U (-infinity, 12]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

[`18*2+2`] is equal to [_____]{Real(38.)}
---

What is the value of [`12+17-17/4`]? [_____]{24.75}
---

[`12+16+2+6`] is equal to [_____]{36}
---

What is the value of [`17+5+16+8`]? [_____]{Formula('46')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -7, 8, 9, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 12\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 10\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -4\}`]
- [`C = \{-4, 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup C \cup B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup (((A \cup A))) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, -2, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, -9, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, -9, -5>") x Compute("<-5, -2, 0>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, -9, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, -2, 0>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, -9, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -2, 0>") . Compute("<8, -9, -5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, -9, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 8, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, -4, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, 8, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 8, -10>") . Compute("<9, -4, -4>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 8, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -4, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -4, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -4, -4>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>0)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
